{
  "dom_id": "step-e5669",
  "name": "Example: Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient of Factorials",
  "problem": "Given that $n \\geq 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac {n!} {(n - 2)!}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\nn! = n \\cdot (n-1) \\cdot (n-2)!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-2)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac {n!} {(n - 2)!} \n&= \\dfrac {n \\cdot (n - 1) \\cdot (n - 2)!} {(n - 2)!}\\[5pt] \n\n&= \\dfrac {n \\cdot (n - 1) \\cdot \\cancel{(n - 2)!}} {\\cancel{(n - 2)!}}\\[5pt] \n\n&= n(n -1) \\[5pt]\n&= n^2 - n\n\t}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
